hadiths[27]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20555","Waki' narrated to us, Sawadah ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any shepherd entrusted with a flock who deceives it is in the Fire."
"20556","Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I heard Isma'il al-Basri narrating from the daughter of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from her father Ma'qil, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no ruler of a community, small or large, who does not act justly among them, except that Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, will throw him on his face into the Fire."
"20557","Isma'il narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Ma'qil ibn Yasar fell ill, and 'Abdullah ibn Ziyad entered upon him, meaning to visit him, and he said: Indeed I shall narrate to you a hadith I had not narrated to you: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, does not entrust a servant with a flock and he dies on the day he dies while deceiving it, except that Allah forbids Paradise to him."
"20558","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj informed us, Shu'bah informed us, he said: I heard 'Iyad Abu Khalid, he said: I saw two men disputing before Ma'qil ibn Yasar, and Ma'qil ibn Yasar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby a man's property will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"20559","'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn 'Abdullah al-A'raj, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of al-Hudaybiyah while he was holding up a branch of a tree with his hand above the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as the people pledged allegiance; they pledged allegiance to him not to flee, and on that day they were one thousand four hundred."
"20560","'Abdullah narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj: The hand of Allah is above their hands. He said: Not to flee."
"20561","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, 'Iyad Abu Khalid narrated to me, he said: There was talk between two neighbors of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, and the oath fell upon one of them, so I heard Ma'qil ibn Yasar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby his brother's property will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"20562","Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Isma'il, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to us, from Isma'il al-Awdi, from the daughter of Ma'qil al-Muzani, she said: When my father grew heavy, Ibn Ziyad came to him, and he drove it, meaning he drove the hadith."
"20563","Waki' narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dalham narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that a man from the Ansar married a woman and her hair fell out, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about hair extensions, and he cursed the woman who adds hair and the woman to whom it is added."
"20564","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad al-Qirdusi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar al-Muzani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Work during turmoil is like emigration to me."
"20565","'Abd al-Samad and 'Affan said, al-Muthanna ibn 'Awf narrated to us, Abu 'Abdullah al-Jasri narrated to us, he said: I asked Ma'qil ibn Yasar about drink, and he said: We were in Madinah, and it had abundant dates, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us fadikh, and a man came to him and asked him about an old aged mother of his: Shall we give her nabidh to drink, for she does not eat food? So Ma'qil forbade him."
"20566","'Arim narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from a man, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Al-Baqarah is the hump of the Qur'an and its peak; with every verse of it eighty angels descended, and There is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer was extracted from beneath the Throne and joined to it, or: joined to Surah al-Baqarah; and Ya-Sin is the heart of the Qur'an; no man recites it seeking Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, and the Hereafter, except that he is forgiven; and recite it over your dead."
"20567","'Arim narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman, and he is not al-Nahdi, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Recite it over your dead, meaning Ya-Sin."
"20568","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn 'Atiyyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Rabab, he said: I heard Ma'qil ibn Yasar say: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey of his, and we stopped in a place abundant in garlic, and some Muslims took some of it, then they came to the prayer place to pray with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he forbade them it; then they came after that to the prayer place, and he forbade them it; then they came after that to the prayer place, and he forbade them it; then they came after that to the prayer place, and he found its smell from them, and said: Whoever eats of this tree, let him not approach us in our mosque."
"20569","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Hanafi Abu 'Azzah al-Dabbagh narrated to us, from Abu al-Rabab, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey of his, then he mentioned its meaning."
"20570","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abu Ya'qub, meaning Ishaq ibn 'Uthman, narrated to us, Humran or Hamdan, freedman of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, narrated to me, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: I accompanied the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so and so."
"20571","al-Hakam ibn Nafi' Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Shaybah Yahya ibn Yazid, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Nufay' ibn al-Harith, from Ma'qil al-Muzani, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me to judge among a people, and I said: I do not know how to judge well, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Allah is with the judge so long as he does not deviate deliberately."
"20572","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Khalid, meaning Ibn Tahman Abu al-'Ala' al-Khaffaf, narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi' narrated to me, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever says in the morning three times: I seek refuge with Allah, the Hearing, the Knowing, from the accursed Satan, and recites the last three verses of Surah al-Hashr, Allah entrusts to him seventy thousand angels who pray for him until evening; if he dies that day he dies a martyr; and whoever says it in the evening is in that same station."
"20573","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Khalid, meaning Ibn Tahman, narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi', from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: I performed ablution for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day, and he said: Do you wish to visit Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her? I said: Yes. So he stood leaning on me and said: Indeed another than you will carry her burden, and its reward will be yours. He said: It was as if nothing was upon me until we entered upon Fatimah, peace be upon her, and he said to her: How do you find yourself? She said: By Allah, my grief has intensified, my need has intensified, and my illness has prolonged. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting concerning this hadith, he said: Are you not pleased that I married you to the earliest of my ummah in submission, the most knowledgeable of them, and the greatest of them in forbearance?"
"20574","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Injustice will not remain after me except a little, until it appears; whenever anything of injustice appears, as much of justice departs, until one is born in injustice who knows nothing else; then Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, will bring justice; whenever anything of justice comes, as much of injustice departs, until one is born in justice who knows nothing else."
"20575","'Amr ibn al-Haytham Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from his father, from 'Amr ibn Maymun: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, witnessed - and he had gathered the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his lifetime and health - and adjured them by Allah: Who heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention anything concerning the grandfather? So Ma'qil ibn Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, brought an inheritance case in which there was a grandfather, and he gave him a third or a sixth. He said: And what is the inheritance case? He said: I do not know. He said: What prevented you from knowing?"
"20576","'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab asked about the ordinance of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the grandfather, so Ma'qil ibn Yasar al-Muzani stood and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed concerning it. He said: What? He said: A sixth. He said: With whom? He said: I do not know. He said: You have not known, so what use are you then?"
"20577","Yazid narrated to us, Mustalim ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Worship during tribulation is like emigration to me."
"20578","'Abd al-Samad and Hasan said, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from a man, he is al-Hasan if Allah wills, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: Nothing was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than horses. Then he said: O Allah, forgiveness; no, rather women."
"20579","'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Murrah Abu al-Mu'alla, narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: Ma'qil ibn Yasar grew heavy, and 'Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad entered to him to visit him, and said: Do you know, O Ma'qil, that I have shed blood? He said: I do not know. He said: Do you know that I have entered into anything of Muslim prices? He said: I do not know. He said: Seat me. Then he said: Listen, O 'Ubaydullah, until I narrate to you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not once nor twice: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever enters into anything of Muslim prices to raise it against them, then it is a right upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, to seat him in a great mass of Fire on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, more than once or twice."
"20580","'Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, and 'Attab narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu 'Uthman, and he is not al-Nahdi, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Recite it over your dead. 'Ali ibn Ishaq said in his hadith: Meaning Ya-Sin."
"20581","Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: Ma'qil ibn Yasar fell ill with an illness in which he grew heavy, and Ibn Ziyad came to visit him, and he said: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever is entrusted with a flock and does not surround them with counsel will not find the scent of Paradise, and its scent is found from a distance of a hundred years. Ibn Ziyad said: Why did you not narrate this to me before now? He said: And now, were it not for the state you are in, I would not have narrated it to you."
